### Concurrency

- Never subscribe inside a `subscribe` callback; compose with `switchMap`, `mergeMap`, or `toSignal` instead.
<!-- Project-specific / Angular-Concurrency -->

### Components

- Write standalone components, directives, and pipes; declare one in an `NgModule` only where the surrounding code is still module-based.
- Inject collaborators with `inject()` or the constructor; never `new` a service directly.
<!-- Project-specific / Angular-Components -->

### State

- Hold state in `signal()`, derive it with `computed()`, and accept it through `input()`/`model()`; never derive a value into a second signal that `computed()` should own.
- Write every component to work without Zone.js and under `OnPush`: change state through signals and inputs, never by mutating an object in place and waiting for the view to notice.
- Use `effect()` only to synchronize with something outside Angular's reactivity; a template or a computed signal answers most other needs.
<!-- Project-specific / Angular-State -->

### Templates

- Keep templates free of method calls that carry business logic; bind to a signal or a getter that calls the one function that owns the rule.
- Track list items by stable data identity (`track item.id` in `@for`, `trackBy` in `*ngFor`), never the index when order can change.
<!-- Project-specific / Angular-Templates -->
